    "result_text": "The full build passes. All tests are green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented telephone normalization on owner creation (`POST /api/owners`), handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Relaxed the `telephone` DTO constraint by removing the strict `^[0-9]*$` pattern (and widening `maxLength` to 30) so raw input containing separators like `(04) 1234-5678` reaches the controller instead of being rejected by bean validation before normalization can occur.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 Added a `normalizeTelephone` step that strips every non-digit character (`replaceAll(\"\\\\D\", \"\")`) and requires exactly 10 digits; the normalized 10-digit value is stored on the DTO before mapping, so it is what gets persisted and returned. If the stripped result isn't exactly 10 digits, it throws `InvalidTelephoneException`.\n\n3. **`InvalidTelephoneException`** (new) + handler in **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 Maps the failure to a `400 Bad Request` with `telephone` reported in the `errors` array, consistent with the existing validation-error style.\n\nThe entity's existing `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{10}$\")` / `@Digits` constraints remain and are satisfied by the normalized value.\n\n**Test results:** `AcceptanceTest` (the only test class with `@Test` methods) \u2014 both `coreStripsToTenDigits` (`(04) 1234-5678` \u2192 stored `0412345678`) and `errorRejectsTooFewDigits` (`12345` \u2192 400) pass; `BUILD SUCCESS` for the full suite.",
